│ Okay, let’s address this issue. The core     │
│ problem is that the py:method directive in   │
│ Sphinx is incorrectly generating parentheses │
│ around the method name. This is likely due   │
│ to how Sphinx is interpreting the :property: │
│ option in conjunction with the py:method     │
│ directive. The :property: option seems to be │
│ causing an unnecessary addition of           │
│ parentheses.                                 │
│                                              │
│ Reasoning:                                   │
│                                              │
│ The issue stems from Sphinx’s documentation  │
│ generation process. The :property: option,   │
│ when used with py:method, appears to be      │
│ triggering an unwanted formatting rule that  │
│ adds parentheses around the method name. The │
│ simplest solution is to remove the           │
│ parentheses. This should resolve the visual  │
│ inconsistency in the generated               │
│ documentation.                               │
│                                              │
│ Patch:                                       │
│                                              │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
│ ┃              modification 1              ┃ │
│ ┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛ │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│  [file][original]# index.rst\n.. py:method:  │
│  Foo.bar\n:property:\n.. py:property::       │
│  Foo.baz\n[/original]\n[patched]#            │
│  index.rst\n.. py:method::                   │
│  Foo.bar\n:property:\n.. py:property::       │
│  Foo.baz\n[/patched]                         │
│                                              │
│                                              │
